From f11c4cf77dc90f57aac89c956b5c81e7c69dde5d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Zambia Treasury Insight <patch@local>
Date: Tue, 24 Nov 2026 19:17:28 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 11/12] Tier 3 #11: Next.js + Plotly React frontend scaffold
 (parallel UI)
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Adds a frontend/ directory containing a Next.js 16 + TypeScript + Tailwind 4
scaffold that serves as a parallel UI for the FastAPI backend. The existing
vanilla-JS static/index.html continues to be served unchanged.

What's here:
  - package.json with Next 16, React 19, react-plotly.js, @tanstack/react-query,
    Tailwind 4, lucide-react
  - lib/api.ts: typed API client wrapping all 17 backend endpoints with Basic
    Auth support and TanStack Query-friendly signatures
  - app/layout.tsx: root layout with the 8-tab sidebar (Overview, Explain,
    History, Forecast, Scenario, Model docs, Audit log, Data & quality)
  - app/page.tsx: working Overview tab that fetches /api/status + /api/overview
    and renders the data-mode banner + per-series cards with 1w/4w/12w/52w
    change
  - app/globals.css: Tailwind 4 with light/dark CSS variables
  - MIGRATION.md: build order for the remaining 7 tabs + shared chart
    components + deploy instructions for Vercel/Render
  - README.md: quick start + deploy + switch-over plan

To run locally:
  cd frontend && npm install && npm run dev
  # or: NEXT_PUBLIC_API_URL=http://localhost:8000 npm run dev

To deploy: push to Vercel, set NEXT_PUBLIC_API_URL to the Render URL, deploy.

The migration is reversible — the vanilla JS UI stays in the repo as a fallback.
