+# Next.js frontend for Zambia Treasury Insight
+
+A parallel Next.js + TypeScript + Tailwind 4 + react-plotly.js frontend for the
+FastAPI backend. The existing vanilla-JS dashboard at `static/index.html` continues
+to be served by FastAPI unchanged; this Next.js app is a separate deployable UI.
+
+## Quick start
+
+```bash
+cd frontend
+npm install
+
+# Develop against the live Render backend:
+npm run dev
+
+# Or against a local FastAPI on :8000:
+NEXT_PUBLIC_API_URL=http://localhost:8000 npm run dev
+```
+
+## What's here
+
+- **`lib/api.ts`** — typed API client wrapping all 17 backend endpoints with
+  Basic Auth support and TanStack Query-friendly signatures.
+- **`app/layout.tsx`** — root layout with the 8-tab sidebar.
+- **`app/page.tsx`** — Overview tab (working reference implementation).
+- **`app/globals.css`** — Tailwind 4 with light/dark CSS variables.
+
+See **`MIGRATION.md`** for the build order of the remaining 7 tabs and the
+shared chart components.
+
+## Deploy
+
+The Next.js app is deployed separately from the FastAPI backend. The cleanest
+option is Vercel:
+
+1. Push `frontend/` to its own repo (or keep as a subdir).
+2. Import into Vercel.
+3. Set `NEXT_PUBLIC_API_URL=https://zambia-treasury-insight.onrender.com`.
+4. Deploy.
+
+## Switching over from the vanilla JS UI
+
+The FastAPI backend continues to serve `static/index.html` at `/` until you're
+ready to switch. To switch:
+
+1. Complete the remaining 7 tabs per `MIGRATION.md`.
+2. Deploy the Next.js app.
+3. Update `app/main.py`'s `index()` route to redirect `/` to the Next.js URL,
+   or remove it and serve only the API from FastAPI.
+
+The migration is reversible — the vanilla JS UI stays in the repo as a fallback.
